<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yugoslav Partisans</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yugoslav Partisans were the Communist-led resistance movement in occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, commanded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josip-broz-tito">Josip Broz Tito</a>. They rose in July 1941, briefly holding the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzice">Užice</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and much of Montenegro, and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> armies, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ustase">Ustaše</a> and the royalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chetniks">Chetniks</a>. By 1945 they had liberated most of the country and formed the core of socialist Yugoslavia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yugoslav-partisans.jpg" alt="Yugoslav Partisans" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Yugoslavia_(1943%E2%80%931946).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
